## 7. Exact active slice: compute-exchange mutation review

### 7.1 Confirmed root defect and correction

The first mutation cohort exposed a real legal-configuration fail-stop defect.
One settle/refill exchange owns two independent linear partitions:

```text
completion capabilities <= P
refill grants            <= P
valid aggregate          <= 2P
```

`P` is the configured active-work/worker topology. The old code summed both
partitions and compared the result with the unrelated fixed membership/RBF
component bound 100. A legal worker topology could therefore raise
`SchedulerProjection` and stop the service.

The correction:

- exposes `ResourceLimits::active_work_limit()`;
- checks each partition independently against `P`;
- adds no state, lock, task, queue, retry or repair path;
- updates the I3 math and architecture complexity table;
- adds exact tests for legal `P > 100` grants and stale completions, mutation-
  free rejection of either `P + 1` partition and malformed/nonmalformed verify
  peer-revocation behavior.

Focused Nextest run `19fb2cd1-848b-4c78-bee4-66bd90e8c603` passed all 17
compute-exchange tests. Formatting and diff checks passed.

Migration validation found that the four tests introduced by this correction
had not yet been connected to the machine review graph. They now map to the
existing `TP-WORKER-001` and `TP-ADMIN-001` behaviors and invariants, and the
generated review guide and test inventory were regenerated. This is evidence
wiring, not a new behavior, production state or correction.

